  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "E31-1",
      "fact": "Standalone coordinator begins registry record before readiness. Registry keys (runId,messageId); dedupeKey is stored, not a second unique index. Current terminal TTL is 15 minutes; outstanding records do not expire. Module documentation states at least 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "E31-2",
      "fact": "Team and Org strict SEND_MESSAGE keep message_id/dedupe_key, use root membership/lease/readiness and configured handle. Org command_id correlates transport ACK but is not passed into message metadata. Configured handle calls AgentRun.postUserMessage without registry begin."
    },
    {
      "id": "E31-3",
      "fact": "AgentRun serialized postUserMessage admits each invocation and claims recovery from its new sequence. AdmissionState reserves every invocation anew; removeEntry forgets settled entries. Pending-only dedupe cannot cover completed/rejected identities."
    },
    {
      "id": "E31-4",
      "fact": "Configured handle publishes member_input for every accepted result; Team/Org handlers record activity for accepted input. A dedupe result that only returns accepted=true would duplicate presentation/activity unless disposition is propagated. Team has no positive SEND_MESSAGE ACK; Org has existing accepted/rejected/failed correlated ACK; standalone has duplicate_* states."
    },
    {
      "id": "E31-5",
      "fact": "ActivationRegistry enforces one current run per runId and resource release checks exact expectedRun; supports explicit removal/inactive discovery/replacement/stop/rollback. Reuse that identity-qualified cleanup for registry live pin, not stream-disconnect cleanup."
    },
    {
      "id": "E31-6",
      "fact": "IR004 existing deterministic evidence uses actual strict handlers/configured handle/AgentRun/native core with synthetic strategy and test-owned root hosting. Two ordinary fresh controls pass; two duplicate B cases fail (operation2 ->3, [A,B]->[A,B,B]). This round reads/reconciles results; no test rerun or full-root acceptance claim."
    }
  ],
